","20271225","20280101","20280117"],"facts":["The Ferry operates between the St. George Ferry Terminal on Staten Island and the Whitehall Terminal in Lower Manhattan. The trip is free and takes about 25 minutes. The ferry does not carry cars.","A 5.2-mile run, 24 hours a day, 365 days a year.","Over 16 million passengers a year.","On a typical weekday, five boats make 117 trips, carrying approximately 45,000 passengers.","During rush hours the ferry runs on a four-boat schedule, with 15 minutes between departures.","On weekends, three boats make 96 trips across the harbor each day.","The boats make over 40,000 trips a year.","Annual on-time performance in 2023 was 96%.","The City has operated the Staten Island Ferry since 1905."],"fleet":[{"class":"Ollis","boats":["Staff Sergeant Michael H. Ollis","Sandy Ground","Dorothy Day"],"passengers":4500},{"class":"Molinari","boats":["Guy V. Molinari","Sen. Marchi","Spirit of America"],"passengers":4427},{"class":"Barberi","boats":["Samuel I. Newhouse"],"passengers":5200},{"class":"Austen","boats":2,"passengers":1107}]}